ly vm` path for kubevirt** — a kubevirt deploy is brought up by the\nplugin'\''s deploy lifecycle, not `charly vm build`.\n\n## Two ways to see it\n\n1. **As a VM-shaped venue** — a `kind: kubevirt` entity is a `#KubeVirt` template\n   (source, machine, guest, network, instancetype, migration, snapshot, GPU); the\n   plugin renders it to a KubeVirt `VirtualMachine` CR, applies it, waits for the\n   VMI `Ready` + the guest agent `Connected`, opens a managed `virtctl\n   port-forward` to guest SSH on an auto-allocated local port, and records the\n   venue identity as `kubevirt_state` in the per-host overlay. Guest-side plan\n   walks then run over that SSH executor — the SAME `sdk/kit.WalkPlans` seam\n   `deploy:vm` uses. The declared `DeployTraits` are\n   `{Venue:\"ssh\", ImageBacked:true, BedTarget:true, SupportsEphemeral:true,\n   SupportsFromSnapshot:true}` with **no** `ExclusiveVenue` (a KubeVirt VM is a\n   cluster-managed workload, so no host arbiter).\n2. **As a `charly kubevirt` CLI family** — `build`/`create` (render vs apply a\n   VirtualMachine from a `kind: kubevirt` entity), `start`/`stop`/`restart`/\n   `destroy`, `console` (virtctl serial), `ssh` (print the managed alias),\n   `snapshot` (VirtualMachineSnapshot CR), `migrate`\n   (VirtualMachineInstanceMigration), `gpu` (show the devices an entity would\n   request), `status` (live VMs). The plugin owns the whole Kong grammar AND the\n   CR operations, built on the SAME cluster_ops surface the verb uses (R3).\n\n## Authoring (sketch)\n\n```yaml\nversion: 2026.261.1747\nkubevirt:\n    vm:\n        kind: kubevirt\n        source:\n            container_disk:\n                image: ghcr.io/opencharly/arch-vm:latest\n        machine: { cpus: 2, memory: 2Gi }\n        guest: { user: arch }\n        ssh: { user: arch }\n    prod:\n        target: kubevirt\n        from: kubevirt.vm          # template cross-ref, or an inline kind: kubevirt node\n        cluster: prod              # a kind: kubernetes cluster template name\n        namespace: vms\n```\n\n## The verb and the beds\n\nThe declarative `kubevirt:` check verb (see `/charly-kubevirt:check-kubevirt`)\nprobes a running cluster (vm/vmi/wait-ready/guest-info/datavolume/snapshot/\nmigration). The platform install is `candy/kubevirt-operator`\n(`/charly-kubevirt:kubevirt-operator`); the client is `candy/kubevirt` (virtctl).\nThe R10 beds are `check-kubevirt-operator` (KubeVirt + CDI onto a k3s VM) and\n`check-kubevirt-vm` (a charly-built VM box booted as a `containerDisk`, guest SSH\nover the port-forward, then a fresh `charly update`).\n","triggers":["KubeVirt / `kind: kubevirt` / a `kubevirt:` or `target: kubevirt` deploy / `deploy:kubevirt` / running a charly VM on a Kubernetes cluster","`charly kubevirt` CLI (build/create/start/stop/restart/destroy/console/ssh/snapshot/migrate/gpu/status) / the VirtualMachine CR lifecycle"],"category":"kind"},{"family":"kubevirt","name":"kubevirt-operator","owner":"plugin-kubevirt","description":"KubeVirt + CDI platform install on a Kubernetes cluster — the `candy/kubevirt-operator` layer downloads the pinned operator + CR manifests and applies them with the `kube:` verb, then waits for the KubeVirt/CDI CRs with the `kubevirt:` verb. Use before installing KubeVirt on a k3s/kind/kubernetes venue, authoring the platform leg of a kubevirt bed, or authoring the kubevirt-vm cluster entity.","content":"# layer-kubevirt-operator — the KubeVirt + CDI platform install\n\n`candy/kubevirt-operator` (standalone repo `opencharly/layer-kubevirt-operator`)\nturns a Kubernetes cluster into a virtualization platform. It:\n\n1. `download:`s the pinned `kubevirt-operator.yaml` + `kubevirt-cr.yaml`\n   (github.com/kubevirt/kubevirt releases) and `cdi-operator.yaml` + `cdi-cr.yaml`\n   (github.com/kubevirt/containerized-data-importer releases);\n2. applies them with the `kube:` check verb (`method: apply`);\n3. waits for the KubeVirt CR to report `Deployed` via the `kubevirt:` verb\n   (`method: wait-ready`).\n\nIt runs in a venue that ALREADY has a cluster reachable via kubeconfig — a\n`k3s-server` VM, a `kindcluster`, or a `target: kubernetes` host. It uses only\nexisting charly verbs (`kube:` apply + the `kubevirt:` wait probe) — no new\nmechanism, no ad-hoc `kubectl`.\n\nThe client candy is `candy/kubevirt` (virtctl at `/usr/bin/virtctl`). The R10\nconsumers are the `check-kubevirt-operator` and `check-kubevirt-vm` beds.\n","triggers":["installing KubeVirt + CDI on a cluster / `candy/kubevirt-operator` / the kubevirt platform leg of a check bed"],"category":"commands"}]'
